tensions in the Gulf region were already  high in this instant has raised them  again according to US defense officials  the instant happened at the northern  entrance of the Straits of Hormuz near  the island of abu musa now the strait is  a vital shipping route linking Middle  East oil producers to markets in the  rest of the world it is just over a  hundred miles long but only 21 miles  wide at its narrowest point and the  shipping lanes are just two miles wide  in either direction so it's a real  potential pinch point daily oil flow in  the Strait of Hormuz averaged 21 million  barrels per day last year that's about a  third of all the oil that was  transported and traded by sea around the  globe now the waters around the island  of abu musa are hotly contested but abu  musa and those waters are controlled by  Iran and according to the Ministry of  Defense the Royal Navy frigate HMS Mont  Rose which was shadowing the British  heritage oil tanker from a distance was  forced to move between the tanker and  the three Iranian boats when they tried  to bring the tanker to a halt as it was  moving into international waters  HMS Montrose is a well armed vessel with  a 4.5 inch main gun and missile system  and a wildcat helicopter on board which  did deploy in this incident the raw Navy  also has in addition to that frigate for  mine hunters and a Royal Fleet Auxiliary  support ship already stationed in a  permanent Naval Support Facility at  mineral man in Bahrain America has an  aircraft carrier the USS Abraham Lincoln  operating in the Gulf of Oman and as  well as a range of other naval assets  the USS boxer is currently in the Gulf  of Aden but this latest incident as well  as escalating tension may add calls to  create a multinational coalition to  safeguard these vital international  waters
 

